{"id":"split-level-concept","version":1,"category":"tradition","when":"Use when the brief or chosen programme calls for split level residential concept.","title":"Split level residential concept","combinations":"Use the supported neutral palette to reinforce hierarchy; avoid suggesting unavailable textures.","placement":"Connect adjacent occupied datums with explicit landings and composed steps.","principles":"Generation remains on flat terrain and does not simulate hillside foundations.","capabilities":"Use direct-scene primitives: plate, wall, roof, entrance. No change-of-use approval, occupancy calculation, acoustic or accessibility certification.","sources":[{"reference":"src/lib/villa/scene/terra.ts","kind":"repository","verified":true,"note":"Checked primitive names against the direct-scene contract; individually curated conceptual relationships, not external research or a regulation."}],"construction":{"operations":["add","attach","place-on","finish"],"requiredKinds":["plate","wall","roof","entrance"],"materials":"Use the supported neutral palette to reinforce hierarchy; avoid suggesting unavailable textures.","supports":"Build occupied room shells and circulation specific to the requested use before exterior details.","unsupported":"No change-of-use approval, occupancy calculation, acoustic or accessibility certification."}}
