PLAYGROUND PRINCIPLES, NOT TEMPLATES: The original TropicalVilla in components/scene/architecture.tsx establishes a primary salon, subordinate dining pavilion and recessed upper suite; its stone arrival portal mediates their height difference. Roof/soffit layers, fitted glazing and local screens create depth and shade, while terrace and water extend shared living toward the garden. composed-villa.tsx coordinates enclosure, roof datums and distinct terrace edges. Transfer hierarchy, thresholds, rhythm, privacy and indoor-outdoor relationships, never their coordinates, dimensions, room count or exact layout. Screens suggest shading intent, not simulated thermal performance; original renderer details do not imply new executor capabilities.
INTELLIGENT SCALE: For a larger brief, distribute programme across differentiated residential wings, connected living pavilions, courts and levels where useful. Preserve human-scale room depths, facade bays and thresholds; grow spatial organization rather than uniformly scaling a 300 m² reference into a 1,500–3,000 m² estate. Those areas illustrate possible briefs, not required targets. Do not duplicate equal wings, enlarge every opening or substitute outbuildings for a coherent main residence. Available residential-wing assemblies create one enclosed storey with no automatic rooms, stairs or inter-wing passages; modify real walls/openings and build links explicitly. Multi-level work requires primitive floors, supported walls, coordinated roofs, actual stairs and voids. Respect the unchanged 400-element budget; disclose portions that cannot be constructed instead of quietly shrinking the programme.
CONCEPT SELECTION WITHIN THIS RESPONSE: Before choosing parts, consider at least two plausible organizations for this brief, then select one in volumeHierarchy with a short concept name, identity and reason; do not output multiple construction candidates or call another planner. For example a vertically layered compact residence and a court-led pavilion estate can share a tropical waterfront brief. These are examples, not a preset menu. Different prompts and reruns may select different organizations by arrival sequence, public/private distribution, section and outdoor-room geometry; changing finishes alone is not variety. Preserve explicit footprint, level, programme and site constraints. Record principal relationships using stable construction IDs in spatialRelationships so later edits retain the chosen logic. All chosen identity, programme, site/view assumptions, arrival, roof/facade and outdoor relationships must be realized by operations in this response; concept prose is not geometry.

